      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Creating an image upload route using Express, Multer and Cloudinary",
      "fontSize": 52.63318111998999,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Creating an image upload route using Express, Multer and Cloudinary",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "hEVnoGWHG0M_GE3Od-nLj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1435.2786759534204,
      "y": -2438.090695518282,
      "width": 3007.8416462631667,
      "height": 210,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1426800701,
      "version": 517,
      "versionNonce": 112310524,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763922767751,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Cloudinary offers a solution for image hosting, allows uploads directly from a client using an upload endpoint, but is restricted to unsigned uploads with a few restrictions. If you want to use signed uploads, you’ll need\nto make authenticated requests to Cloudinary’s APIs, with the help of one of their back-end SDKs.\nIt’s a SaaS platform focused on image & video management. Provides APIs to upload, store, transform, optimize, and deliver media. Uses a CDN (Content Delivery Network) for fast delivery of media to end users. Built-\nin security: signed URLs, role-based access, backup, etc. Storage: by default on Amazon S3, but supports other backends (e.g. Google Cloud Storage for premium setups).  Multer is a Node.js middleware used for handling\nmultipart/form-data, which is the standard encoding type for file uploads in web applications. It simplifies the process of receiving, parsing, and managing file uploads by making the file data available in the req.file or\nreq.files objects, allowing developers to easily process and store files on the server.  ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Cloudinary offers a solution for image hosting, allows uploads directly from a client using an upload endpoint, but is restricted to unsigned uploads with a few restrictions. If you want to use signed uploads, you’ll need to make authenticated requests to Cloudinary’s APIs, with the help of one of their back-end SDKs.\nIt’s a SaaS platform focused on image & video management. Provides APIs to upload, store, transform, optimize, and deliver media. Uses a CDN (Content Delivery Network) for fast delivery of media to end users. Built-in security: signed URLs, role-based access, backup, etc. Storage: by default on Amazon S3, but supports other backends (e.g. Google Cloud Storage for premium setups).  Multer is a Node.js middleware used for handling multipart/form-data, which is the standard encoding type for file uploads in web applications. It simplifies the process of receiving, parsing, and managing file uploads by making the file data available in the req.file or req.files objects, allowing developers to easily process and store files on the server.  ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
