    {
      "id": "3Cez7P0fQ8CtJotV0lvQs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2432.453961548697,
      "y": -1880.7119253758833,
      "width": 871.3258666992188,
      "height": 677.131641152981,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2S",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1973841532,
      "version": 106,
      "versionNonce": 1226728828,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763923697667,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Cloudinary Upload Notes:\n\n1. Direct Upload (Recommended)\n   - When using multer.diskStorage\n   - Upload using: cloudinary.uploader.upload(req.file.path)\n   - Fast, simple, preferred method\n\n2. Data URI Upload (Older / Optional) (we did it here but no need of this)\n   - Converts file buffer to Base64 string\n   - Used mostly when using multer.memoryStorage\n   - Or when receiving Base64 from frontend/mobile apps\n   - Not required for normal uploads\n\n3. Direct Buffer Upload (Better than Data URI)\n   - Cloudinary supports uploading raw buffer directly\n   - Use upload_stream with req.file.buffer\n   - No need for Base64 conversion\n\n4. Summary\n   - diskStorage → direct upload\n   - memoryStorage → buffer upload\n   - Data URI → only needed in special cases, mostly outdated\n",
      "fontSize": 23.552404909668905,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Cloudinary Upload Notes:\n\n1. Direct Upload (Recommended)\n   - When using multer.diskStorage\n   - Upload using: cloudinary.uploader.upload(req.file.path)\n   - Fast, simple, preferred method\n\n2. Data URI Upload (Older / Optional) (we did it here but no need of this)\n   - Converts file buffer to Base64 string\n   - Used mostly when using multer.memoryStorage\n   - Or when receiving Base64 from frontend/mobile apps\n   - Not required for normal uploads\n\n3. Direct Buffer Upload (Better than Data URI)\n   - Cloudinary supports uploading raw buffer directly\n   - Use upload_stream with req.file.buffer\n   - No need for Base64 conversion\n\n4. Summary\n   - diskStorage → direct upload\n   - memoryStorage → buffer upload\n   - Data URI → only needed in special cases, mostly outdated\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
